@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000
@scenarioVersion = 12

### Registro válido -> 201, retorna o usuário criado (sem password)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ada Lovelace",
  "email": "ada.{{scenarioVersion}}@example.com",
  "password": "S3nhaForte!123"
}

### Registro com e-mail duplicado -> 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ada Lovelace",
  "email": "ada.{{scenarioVersion}}@example.com",
  "password": "S3nhaForte!123"
}

### Login válido -> 200, captura o token para os cenários seguintes
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ada.{{scenarioVersion}}@example.com",
  "password": "S3nhaForte!123"
}

### Login com senha errada -> 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ada.{{scenarioVersion}}@example.com",
  "password": "senha-errada"
}

### GET /auth/me com token válido -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### GET /auth/me sem Authorization -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
